{"learner_profile": "Undergraduates familiar with sorted arrays, floor division, asymptotic logarithmic time and loop-invariant reasoning. Their binary-search experience is tracing exact-match searches; they have no practice constructing or proving a lower-bound search, including cases where the loop does not advance.", "student_visible_text": "An array a has at least one element and is sorted in nondecreasing order; duplicates are allowed. Integers and indexing are exact. Given target t, return the smallest index i with a[i] >= t, or len(a) if there is no such index. The following code is proposed:
l = 0
r = len(a) - 1
while l < r:
    m = (l + r) // 2
    if a[m] < t:
        l = m
    else:
        r = m
return l
